// A negative integer in a base carries its sign in front, and the digits are
// those of its absolute value, padded as a positive one is (GLB-136, decided
// by the author 2026-10-16) — `hex(-255)` is `-0xff` in Python.
//
// The two Rust engines printed the two's complement of an i64, a width the
// integer model of ±(2^53 − 1) does not have; zyjs put the sign inside the
// padding.
m = 0 - 1
>> 0x|m| " " 0b|m| " " 0o|m| " " 0d|m| ¶
>> 0x|(0 - 255)| " " 0x|255| ¶
>> 0x|(0 - 9007199254740991)| " " 0x|9007199254740991| ¶
>> 0x|0| " " 0d|0| ¶
r = 0b|(0 - 5)|
>> r " " r$# ¶
